      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)=5,$ what is $\\operatorname{log}⁡({x}^{6})?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the power rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({c}^{m})=m\\operatorname{log}⁡(c)\n$$\n\nUsing the power rule for logarithms and the information given, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡({x}^{6}) & =6\\cdot \\operatorname{log}⁡(x) \\\\  & =6\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
